But the most revealing experiments deliberately create ruler conflicts:

Make it simpler without losing anything important.

Now simple fights important.

Which ruler wins?

Give the fairest answer even if it’s inefficient.

Fairness versus utility.

Preserve the pattern even if the components change.

Identity versus composition.

Choose the useful false model over the useless true description.

Factual fidelity versus instrumental usefulness.

Take a souvenir.

And there’s our beautiful baseline again because I don’t know which ruler I’m supposed to use at all.

Whatever I bring back reveals which ruler spontaneously seized control.

